186045417] [17592186571384 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the statement  $¬(P∨¬Q)$ using De Morgan's laws." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571384 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f35f97f-518c-5bc3-8e7f-b4c49c35520a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571384 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q)≡¬P∨¬Q, \\\\ ¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∨¬Q) & ≡¬P∧¬(¬Q) \\\\  & ≡¬P∧Q\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571388 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571388 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182448" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571388 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571388 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $1$ is not prime and $1$ is not composite.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571388 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3bef771f-b5d0-5c41-9326-f619dd4a81a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571388 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,¬(1\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ and }1\\text{ is not composite}) & ≡¬((1\\text{ is not prime})∧(1\\text{ is not composite})) \\\\  & ≡¬(1\\text{ is not prime})∨¬(1\\text{ is not composite}) \\\\  & ≡(1\\text{ is prime})∨(1\\text{ is composite}) \\\\  & ≡1\\text{ is prime}\\text{ or }1\\text{ is composite}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571400 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571400 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571400 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571400 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $10$ is odd or $10\\,|\\,50.$\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571400 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5839b924-3e8e-5a75-a91d-b04c822d078a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571400 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(10\\text{ is odd}\\text{ or }10\\,|\\,50) & ≡¬((10\\text{ is odd})∨(10\\,|\\,50)) \\\\  & ≡¬(10\\text{ is odd})∧¬(10\\,|\\,50) \\\\  & ≡(10\\text{ is even})∧(10\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,50) \\\\  & ≡10\\text{ is even}\\text{ and }10\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571402 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571402 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571402 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571402 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $0$ is negative or $\\{0\\}$ is not empty.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5efba9b1-d57e-5db5-8d34-ed2dd9f14d2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571402 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(0\\text{ is negative}\\text{ or }\\{0\\}\\text{ is not empty}) & ≡¬((0\\text{ is negative})∨(\\{0\\}\\text{ is not empty})) \\\\  & ≡¬(0\\text{ is negative})∧¬(\\{0\\}\\text{ is not empty}) \\\\  & ≡(0\\text{ is not negative})∧(\\{0\\}\\text{ is empty}) \\\\  & ≡0\\text{ is not negative}\\text{ and }\\{0\\}\\text{ is empty}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571418 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571418 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182620" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571418 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571418 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $P$ is not a rhombus or $Q$ is a rectangle.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571418 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7bb1981d-f208-5e7e-b131-a36bdf5855b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571418 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,¬(P\\text{ is not a rhombus}\\text{ or }Q\\text{ is a rectangle}) & ≡¬((P\\text{ is not a rhombus})∨(Q\\text{ is a rectangle})) \\\\  & ≡¬(P\\text{ is not a rhombus})∧¬(Q\\text{ is a rectangle}) \\\\  & ≡(P\\text{ is a rhombus})∧(Q\\text{ is not a rectangle}) \\\\  & ≡P\\text{ is a rhombus}\\text{ and }Q\\text{ is not a rectangle}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571428 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571428 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129826" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571428 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571428 #edb/ref 1071 "Rewrite the statement $¬(¬A∧(¬B∨A))$ using De Morgan's laws." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571428 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97dcc406-82e2-57c8-880f-2a83c1dc8205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571428 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∨B)≡¬A∧¬B, \\\\ ¬(A∧B)≡¬A∨¬B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬A∧(¬B∨A)) & ≡¬(¬A)∨¬(¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡A∨(¬(¬B)∧¬A) \\\\  & ≡A∨(B∧¬A)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571439 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571439 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571439 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571439 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the statement $¬((Q∧P)∨R)$ using De Morgan's laws." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571439 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7b90018-7b1c-54ba-9ffe-d35b97be0c78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571439 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(Q∧P)≡¬P∨¬R, \\\\ ¬(Q∨P)≡¬P∧¬Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((Q∧P)∨R) & ≡¬(Q∧P)∧¬R \\\\  & ≡(¬Q∨¬P)∧¬R\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571451 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571451 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182441" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571451 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571451 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $x$ is prime and $x$ is odd.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6cb1c6c-0f55-5843-930a-ea6ae4ca9cd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571451 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is prime}\\text{ and }x\\text{ is odd}) & ≡¬((x\\text{ is prime})∧(x\\text{ is odd})) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is prime})∨¬(x\\text{ is odd}) \\\\  & ≡(x\\text{ is not prime})∨(x\\text{ is even}) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ or }x\\text{ is even}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
